    {
      "body": "That all-zero output is actually correct \u2014 it's the **count of missing values remaining after the fill**, so `0` means the fill worked (no NAs left). The previous cell (block 6) showed the counts *before* filling (194, 52, 43, \u2026); block 7 shows them *after*, which is why they're all zero.\n\nThe analysis does use the `dengue` object loaded from the CSV in the \"Load the data\" cell \u2014 I didn't change any loading code. I only had to put the CSV at `data/` because that path was empty; the notebook reads `../data/dengue_features_train.csv`. If you have your own copy of that file you'd rather use, point me to it and I'll swap it in.",
